<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10758" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄντομαι</span></b> , only pres. and
		impf.: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντί,
		ἄντα</span>):—poet. Verb (<i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
			Il.
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντάω</span>
			, <i>meet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.595
			</span></i>, al.; esp. in battle, c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλοισιν ἄντεσθ᾽ ἐν πολέμῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.698
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				16.788
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργύρῳ ἀντομένη . . ἐτράπετ᾽ αἰχμή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.237
				</span></i>
			; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλεπῇ ἤντ. θευμορίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Epigr.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διπλόος ἤντετο
			θώρηξ</span> the breastplate <i>opposed</i> or
			<i>stopped</i> (the dart), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.133
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>meet with favour, greet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.71
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c.acc.pers., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιάζω</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.2
			</span></i>, <i>approach with prayers, entreat,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός σε . . ἄντομαι Διός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1098
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός σε γενειάδος . . ἄντομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					279
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός σ᾽ ὅ τι σοι φίλον ἐκ σέθεν
					ἄντομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					250
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. Ἑρμῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					977
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ὑπέρ τινος</span>
			<i>beg</i> in another's behalf, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				243
			</span></i> (lyr.): abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλθετον, ἀντόμεθ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					1155
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
